
# Manjaro Licensing & Trademark Information

## Software Licensing
Manjaro is a roll-up of thousands of individual software packages. The core infrastructure
 developed by the Manjaro Team (such as build tools, the Pamac package manager, and
 Manjaro-specific scripts) are licensed under various licenses. 

## Individual Packages
As an Arch-based distribution, Manjaro provides software through its repositories and follows
 open-source licensing standards. Licenses for individual packages can be found on a running
 system within the respective package directory under `/usr/share/licenses/` or in the metadata
 of the package manager (`pacman -Qi [package-name]`).

